>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANEKA CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIKI, YASUHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKASHITA, NORIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAKI, AKIRA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIKI YASUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKASHITA NORIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAKI AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIKI, YASUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKASHITA, NORIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAKI, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A processing aid for vinyl chloride resins which comprises a polymer mixture having a specific viscosity  eta sp of 0.5 or higher obtained by emulsion-polymerizing 50 to 99 parts by weight of a monomer mixture (A) consisting mainly of methyl methacrylate to obtain a latex of a (co)polymer having a specific viscosity  eta sp of 0.7 or higher, adding 50 to 1 part by weight of a monomer mixture (B) consisting mainly of one or more (meth)acrylic esters excluding methyl methacrylate to the latex, and polymerizing the monomer mixture (B) in the presence of the latex, the total amount of mixtures (A) and (B) being 100 parts by weight; and a vinyl chloride resin composition which comprises the processing aid and a vinyl chloride resin and gives a (foamed) molding excellent in processability and physical properties.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un auxiliaire de transformation pour résines de chlorure de vinyle, comprenant un mélange polymère ayant une viscosité spécifique  eta sp de 0,5 au moins, obtenu par polymérisation par émulsion de 50 à 99 parties en poids d'un mélange monomère (A) renfermant essentiellement du méthylméthacrylate pour obtenir un latex d'un (co)polymère ayant une viscosité spécifique  eta sp de 0,7 au moins; par addition au latex de 50 à 1 parties en poids d'un mélange monomère (B) renfermant essentiellement un ou plusieurs esters (méth)acryliques, à l'exception du méthylméthacrylate; et par polymérisation du mélange monomère (B) en présence du latex, la quantité totale des mélanges (A) et (B) étant de 100 parties en poids. L'invention concerne également une composition de résine de chlorure de vinyle renfermant l'auxiliaire précité et une résine de chlorure de vinyle. L'auxiliaire de transformation de l'invention confère à un moulage (en produit mousse) d'excellentes propriétés physiques et de transformabilité.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>